# Deep links for the client routes in src/main.jsx.
#
# Destination is "/" not "/index.html": Pages canonicalises /index.html to /,
# which turns a 200 rewrite into a 308 redirect and bounces deep links to the
# homepage.
#
# And NOT a `/*` catch-all: that matches /assets/* too, so an asset request
# that missed at an edge during a deploy came back as 200 text/html instead of
# a 404 — which the /assets/* rule in _headers then marked immutable for a
# year. The edge cached an HTML document under a .css URL and served whoever
# hit that node a completely unstyled page. With no rule matching /assets/*,
# public/404.html answers those with a real 404 instead.
#
# Add a line here whenever a route is added to main.jsx.
/industries/ca-firms  /  200
/industries/solar     /  200
